18:41: error: Wrapped takes type parameters, and deriving for it would need the instance's context worked out from its content - which is a decision this stage has not taken
21:37: error: Bitcast takes 2 type variables, and only a class with one can be derived - there is no single content for a newtype to forward to
24:38: error: Nonexistent is not a class this module can see
27:37: error: AtomicValue is decided structurally and cannot be derived - a newtype is already whatever its content is
41:39: error: Wrapping cannot be derived - its member wrap answers Maybe(a), where the newtype would have to be substituted inside another type; only a bare occurrence can be wrapped
45:37: error: Lending cannot be derived - its member lend answers a borrow, and what a forwarding body would put the newtype's name on is storage the caller already owns
